 ],
 "Site Description": "The ASCA shelf and tall moorings extend 200 km offshore of Hamburg just south of East London on the East coast of South Africa, along the decending TOPEX/Jason satellite ground track # 96, through the core of the Agulhas Current, with Current- and Pressure-recording Inverted Echo Sounders (CPIES) measurements extending the array to 300 km offshore.  There are  two shelf and seven full-depth tall moorings, interspersed with five  CPIES, measuring pressure, current velocities, temperatures and salinities.",
 "Images": [
  "https://deims.org/sites/default/files/photos/agulhas-system-climate-array-south-africa_4623.jpg",
