 "Site Description": "The Jervis Bay Booderee National Park Plot Network is located in Jervis Bay Territory, NSW, Australia and its research infrastructure are structure plots (1 m × 1 m, 20 m × 20 m) nested within 1-ha sites. \r\n\r\nTemporal visits are as follows:\r\n\r\n* Vegetation - 3 years\r\n• Birds - Annual\r\n• Arboreal spotlighting - 2 years\r\n• Reptiles - Annual\r\n• Terrestrial mammals - 2 years\r\n\r\nThe Jervis Bay Booderee National Park Plot Network was a member of Long Term Ecological Research Network (LTERN), Australia, a facility of the Australian Government's Terrestrial Ecosystem Research Network (TERN).",
 "Images": [
