 "Site Name": "Black Sea",
 "Web Links": [
  "https://deims.org/f4193165-b4de-4dc0-a5bd-7f051be25884",
  "http://www.io-bas.bg/",
  "http://www.lter-bulgaria.net/wordpress/en/black-sea/"
 ],
 "Site IDs": [
  "BS",
  "https://deims.org/f4193165-b4de-4dc0-a5bd-7f051be25884"
 ],
 "Site Description": "Black Sea site includes three areas: cape Kaliakra, cape Galata and Varna Bay, and Koketrays Sand bank (only for macrozoobenthos). They were chosen on the base of historical data availability and eutrophication/pollution impact. Kaliakra marine area is influenced by eutrophication due to mainly the Danube river inflow. The local anthropogenic impact in the region is insignificant. It is a nature reserve. Cape Galata and Varna Bay sites are under the indirect impact of Varna Bay current and the system Beloslav lake-Varna lake - a cascade introducing nutrients and pollutants of industrial (chemical industry), agricultural, sewage origin and nearby ports. Koketrays Sand bank is an unique benthic habitat.   \r\nThe coordinates of the selected areas are as follow:\r\nc. Kaliakra: 28.416667\t43.366667\r\nc. Galata:   27.933889\t43.186111\r\nVarna Bay:   28.166667\t43.166667\r\nKoketrays bank: 27.888889 42.635556",
 "Images": [
  "https://deims.org/sites/default/files/photos/black-sea-bulgaria_4966.jpg",
  "https://deims.org/sites/default/files/photos/black-sea-bulgaria_4967.jpg"
 ],
