 ],
 "Site Description": "The site is located in Clocaenog Forest in North East Wales (53o 03’ 19’’N -03o 27’ 55’’ W). It is a typical upland west-atlantic moorland, dominated by the evergreen shrub Calluna vulgaris (heather). Heather makes up >60% of the plant biomass at the site, but Vaccinium myrtillus and Empetrum nigrum are also present.",
 "Images": [
  "https://deims.org/sites/default/files/photos/clocaenog-long-term-monitoring-site-climate-change-research-_5209.jpg"
 ],
