 "Site Description": "The measuring site is located 100 m east of Arctic Station, Qeqertarsuaq, at a mesic heath tundra, Osterlien. Arctic Station is a permanently manned research station operated by the University of Copenhagen on Disko Island, West Greenland. The eddy covariance and climate stations has been operated since 2012, with minor changes in the configureation and setup.",
