 "Site Name": "Las Majadas de Tiétar",
 "Web Links": [
  "https://deims.org/aa0eca4c-528e-4381-9d54-9b441003bc7a"
 ],
 "Site IDs": [
  "https://deims.org/aa0eca4c-528e-4381-9d54-9b441003bc7a"
 ],
 "Site Description": "Las Majadas de Tietar study site (ICOS code ES-LMa) is a holm oak savanna, in Spain. It is located in the province of Caceres. The long-term historical management at the site has resulted in a holm oak (Quercus Ilex) savanna with a tree density of ca. 20-25 trees per hectare, a canopy cover fraction of about 20%, with a mean tree height of 8 m and a mean DBH of 44 cm. The understory vegetation is dominated by annual herbaceous species (as Vulpia bromoides (L.) SF Grey; Vulpia geniculata (L.) Link; Trifolium subterraneum (L.), Ornithopus compressus (L.)) with high biodiversity of species. Herbaceous plants senesce typically by the end of May and re-green mid-October.",
 "Metadata Created": "2024-09-11T10:44:27+02:00",
 "Metadata Updated": "2024-09-12T16:53:23+02:00",
 "Country": [
  "Spain"
 ],
 "Elevation": 265,
 "Coordinates": "POINT (-3.581543 40.279002)",
