  "https://deims.org/26cfa0da-c5bc-489f-8490-beee0e79a9de"
 ],
 "Site Description": "The Strengbach Watershed is a granitic watershed (80ha) located in NE of France, in the Vosges Mountains at altitudes between 880 and 1150 m (omsl) and with highly incised side slopes (mean 15°).\r\nThis catchment is situated in a remote area lacking human activities except forest management.\r\nThe forest covers 90% of the area and corresponds about to 80% spruce (mainly Piceas Abies L.) and 20% beech (Fagus Sylvatica). \r\nThe climate is temperate oceanic mountainous.\r\nThe site is managed by Ecole et Observatoire des Sciences de la Terres (University of Strasbourg / CNRS-INSU-France).",
 "Images": [
  "https://deims.org/sites/default/files/photos/siteVP2.jpg",
  "https://deims.org/sites/default/files/photos/strengbach-watershed-ohge-observatoire-hydro-geochimique-de-lenvironnement-france_6087.png"
 ],
