 ],
 "Site Description": "Hydrometeorological and hydrosedimentary observations within 3 embedded catchments: Gazel, Claduègne and Auzon (3.4, 43, and 116 km²).\r\nMediterranean climate with heavy rainfall and flash floods in automn.\r\nThe upper part of the catchment is characterized by basalt formations, after which a sharp transition occurs where the lower two thirds is made up of sedimentary limestone rock. The soil types are heavily infuenced by the geology of the catchment. \r\nMain land use types are pastures,vineyards and forest.\r\nMore information at http://mistrals.sedoo.fr/?editDatsId=1438",
 "Images": [
  "https://deims.org/sites/default/files/photos/ozcar-ri-ohmcv-auzon-catchment-france_3297.png",
  "https://deims.org/sites/default/files/photos/figure-paysages-auzon.png"
 ],
