 "Site IDs": [
  "KarAq",
  "https://deims.org/0bb608ac-0503-492a-ae5c-97081acabaee"
 ],
 "Site Description": "Aquitain's karsts observatory (Aquitaine, France) regroups different karst sites located on the edge of the Aquitain sedimentary basin. These karst watersheds range from 0.01 km² (Lascaux cave) and 1 km² (Cussac cave) up to 100 km² (Toulon springs) and the land use consists of forests and agriculture under modified oceanic climate. This observatory consists of various observation and experimentation sites like patrimonial caves and large karstic hydrosystem outlets.",
 "Images": [
