  "Rottenhaus_Grabenegg",
  "https://deims.org/a77445b9-6675-4ee1-b3a9-c0722996ef61"
 ],
 "Site Description": "The Grabenegg Field Station (Alpenvorland), Lower Austria, is an agricultural research site of the Austrian Agency for Health and Food Safety (AGES). It is  representative of productive soils managed as arable land. The site is located in the Alpenvorland and the soil described as Gleyic Cambisol (WRB). Cultivated crops and research topics are similar to the site Fuchsenbigl. The following long-term field experiments are still conducted:\r\n• Long term mineral K-fertilisation (since 1954), long-term P fertilisation (different P-forms, since 1954)\r\n• Removal/return of crop residues, P-fertilisation (since 1986)\r\nSoil data, e.g. pH, Corg, Nt, plant available nutrients (P, K), texture, potential N mineralisation, are collected at irregular intervals, crop data each year.",
 "Metadata Created": "2012-12-25T19:06:44+01:00",
 "Metadata Updated": "2025-04-09T08:38:47+02:00",
 "Contact Name": [
