  "Spain ICP-Forests - Plot 05 Ps",
  "https://deims.org/6b5ea4b7-c31d-4418-9dd5-233188df1114"
 ],
 "Site Description": "The Intensive Monitoring of Forest Ecosystems (ICP-Forests Level II network) consists currently in 14 monitoring plots representing important Spanish Forest Ecosystems distributed throughout the Spanish mainland showing the most common forest situations of each country and representing rare or endemic situations.\r\n\r\nThe plot 05 Ps represents an Scots pine (Pinus sylvestris) forest  located in Guadarrama mountain range in the center of the Iberian peninsula.\r\nIt is a 80-100 years old monospecific regular high forest.\r\nUnder a canopy of mature trees, there is an understory made of pines of  about 6 meters high. There is low layer with shrubs and grasses under high cattle pressure.\r\nClimatic gradient is Oromediterranean.\r\nIt is situated in a flat area, with soil temporary swamped in some points.\r\nSoil is made up of gneiss",
 "Images": [
