  "https://deims.org/324f92a3-5940-4790-9738-5aa21992511c"
 ],
 "Site Description": "The LTER grassland sites in the Stubai Valley are situated near the village of Neustift (47° 7′ N, 11° 18′ E). They include a valley bottom meadow at 970 m a.s.l., cut 3-4 times per year, as well as three grasslands differing in land use, which are located on the mountain slope in the vicinity of the Kaserstattalm: a mountain meadow at 1810 m a.s.l. (one cut, lightly grazed in late summer), a pasture at 1870 m a.s.l. and a grassland at 1980 m a.s.l., which was abandoned in 1984. Documentation of management history and vegetation dynamics of the whole area date back to 1865, and detailed information on the current socio-economic situation and future land-use scenarios is available.",
 "Images": [
  "https://deims.org/sites/default/files/photos/burgstall.JPG",
  "https://deims.org/sites/default/files/photos/stubai-combination-neustift-meadows-and-kaserstattalm-austria_4996.jpg",
  "https://deims.org/sites/default/files/photos/stubai-combination-neustift-meadows-and-kaserstattalm-austria_4997.jpg"
 ],
 "Metadata Created": "2012-12-25T19:06:36+01:00",
 "Metadata Updated": "2025-04-09T08:41:32+02:00",
