 ],
 "Site Description": "The sample site of the VULCAN project in Hungary, where research was conducted between 2001 and 2013. We studied the effects of a warming and drying climate on the functioning and organisation of the sand forest-steppe ecosystem. The research activities cover a wide range of areas, including plant phenology, primary productivity, ecophysiology, plant population biology, the role of functional groups, plant biodiversity, biodiversity of specific animal groups, litter decomposition, N-mineralisation, soil respiration, etc.",
 "Metadata Created": "2012-12-25T18:58:02+01:00",
