  "https://deims.org/2d99d848-c4ed-4b20-ac16-3d0f53e1d715"
 ],
 "Site Description": "Research undertaken and supported at WARC is wide ranging and includes archaeology, permafrost, limnology, oceanography, geology, spatial information sciences, botany, renewable energy (solar and wind), atmospheric sciences, wildlife, fisheries, and marine mammal health. Social sciences, health sciences, and traditional knowledge studies are also frequently supported. Each year, we support more than 50 separate research projects. The Aurora Research Institute (ARI) maintains the NWT Research Database, which is a searchable database of all research licenses issued by ARI since 1974.",
